 {"status": "pending", "id": "AUG-165", "title": "[WIRE] Factory wiring: every dispatched worker brief embeds auger spec context --task output", "detail": {"fingerprint": "b45b3b5efcc9a48db2db7116cbf3499c7a3635f9a6c2ad050a58875d5234d919"}, "priority": "P1", "source": null, "reasoning": "The spec context/assemble verbs exist and passed judged runs (AUG-121/122) but NO factory foreman calls them at build time: briefs are still authored from the row text alone. Wire it: on dispatch, the foreman runs `auger spec context --task <row-id>` against the project spec root and embeds the selected blocks (or the structured unscoped/ambiguous answer with its exclusion reasons) in the worker brief.", "review_notes": null, "ts": null, "acceptance_criteria": "A dispatched brief for a task with spec references contains the context-selected blocks verbatim with byte counts; a task with NO spec references produces a brief WITHOUT an empty context section; an ambiguous/unscoped result surfaces in the tick report rather than silently passing. FAILIF: a foreman dispatches a spec-referencing task whose brief lacks the context blocks.", "complexity": 3, "created_at": "2026-11-11T18:54:34.498732+00:00", "updated_at": "2026-11-11T18:54:34.498732+00:00", "foreman_note": null, "capability_tags": [], "depends_on": [], "worker_status": "pending", "commit_hash": null, "guard_result": null, "ci_result": null, "worktree": null, "branch": null}
 {"status": "pending", "id": "AUG-166", "title": "[WIRE] auger serve/api consumed by an external agent at build time", "detail": {"fingerprint": "b805c459fdaab0dbdc01fb4894048cfb078902989a7ca0d1c2d2af4533bf4b16"}, "priority": "P2", "source": null, "reasoning": "AUG-067 shipped the read-first HTTP API and serve ships the embedding store, but no agent other than the authoring seat has ever queried them in anger.", "review_notes": null, "ts": null, "acceptance_criteria": "At least one non-authoring seat (foreman or worker on another project) fetches spec blocks over serve/api during a real task; measured round-trip + bytes recorded on the row; the queried blocks match `spec context` ground truth. FAILIF: the only caller is a hand-run curl by the authoring seat.", "complexity": 3, "created_at": "2026-11-11T18:54:34.530737+00:00", "updated_at": "2026-11-11T18:54:34.530737+00:00", "foreman_note": null, "capability_tags": [], "depends_on": [], "worker_status": "pending", "commit_hash": null, "guard_result": null, "ci_result": null, "worktree": null, "branch": null}
 {"status": "pending", "id": "AUG-167", "title": "[VER] Corpus time-travel: query the spec selection as-of a version", "detail": {"fingerprint": "da54b000c7e3da3946268f126cec1f0b9847ac327069d897a4f095678c7a6345"}, "priority": "P2", "source": null, "reasoning": "Blocks carry version/status (active/deprecated/superseded) but selection can only answer for NOW. Add `spec list/assemble --as-of <tag-or-version>`: resolve the active set as of that ref (git-backed corpus history), superseded blocks resolved to their historical successors.", "review_notes": null, "ts": null, "acceptance_criteria": "As-of an earlier tag, a block edited since returns its OLD text and the new one is absent; as-of HEAD equals plain selection byte-for-byte; an invalid ref answers with a structured error and rc != 0. FAILIF: --as-of silently returns current-day content.", "complexity": 3, "created_at": "2026-11-11T18:54:34.64879+00:00", "updated_at": "2026-11-11T18:54:34.64879+00:00", "foreman_note": null, "capability_tags": [], "depends_on": [], "worker_status": "pending", "commit_hash": null, "guard_result": null, "ci_result": null, "worktree": null, "branch": null}
+{"status": "pending", "id": "REVIEW-AUGER-006", "title": "smoke teardown rmtrees the namespace before checking DELETE status: a 409 orphans the registry row (AUG-117 recurrence)", "detail": {"fingerprint": "b5ea41def1006b6c2ada07f78d12fed32889437a431727fd36866c72a48c341e"}, "priority": "P1", "source": null, "reasoning": "Measured live during the 2026-11-11 review: tests/smoke.sh:62-66 calls auger.delete_namespace(ns, retries=1), then runs shutil.rmtree unconditionally, then inspects the status. On HTTP 409 (substrate lock / non-empty) the directory is destroyed and the mapping survives; the script prints 'teardown skipped'. Both throwaway namespaces from that review are still listed by GET /api/namespaces while only one has a directory on disk. AUG-117 describes this exact failure mode and is marked complete.", "review_notes": null, "ts": null, "acceptance_criteria": "PASS: tests/smoke.sh treats 409 like 429 (bounded backoff, re-enter) and does not call shutil.rmtree unless the DELETE returned 200 or 404. PASS: a run of 'bash tests/smoke.sh <ns>' on a substrate holding a sibling suite's lock leaves zero rows in GET /api/namespaces and zero directories under the substrate root — verified by listing both after the run and quoting the two empty results on the row. PASS: the two existing leftovers (auger-smoke-rv2314, auger-smoke-rvsmoke) are removed and the removal quoted. FAIL: any code path where rmtree runs before the status check.", "complexity": 3, "created_at": "2026-11-12T00:39:50.968237+00:00", "updated_at": "2026-11-12T00:57:00.39653+00:00", "foreman_note": "pytest proof 2026-11-12T00:33Z: the project's own suite reproduces this — 1 failed, 719 passed, 2 skipped, 3 errors in 919.00s. Failure test_no_test_namespace_survives_the_suite + teardown error both say: DELETE returned 409 {'code':'CONFLICT'} 'Push in flight ... Retry after it completes' while tests/test_auger.py retries only 429 and pytest.fail()s otherwise. Fix must cover both paths: the CLI/substrate helper AND the pytest teardown fixture.\n\nregistry census 2026-11-12T00:41Z: GET /api/namespaces lists 34 test-prefixed rows (32 auger-pytest-*, 2 auger-smoke-*); 32 have directories, 2 are registry-only; oldest dir Nov 3 16:39, newest Nov 11 19:55. Nothing reaps them and auger has no delete verb among its 36 subcommands. Acceptance should include draining this backlog, not only stopping new leaks.", "capability_tags": ["teardown", "duckbrain", "smoke", "regression"], "depends_on": [], "worker_status": "pending", "commit_hash": null, "guard_result": null, "ci_result": null, "worktree": null, "branch": null}
+{"status": "pending", "id": "REVIEW-AUGER-007", "title": "one semantic recall costs 9.4s end to end: no query-embedding cache, no progress feedback, so the loop stops being conversational", "detail": {"fingerprint": "64b228d428d68ed0c97715ff0504ad9abd9ab025b0145fcd1f1ace10fc65eb08"}, "priority": "P2", "source": null, "reasoning": "Measured on a free scratch port (47822) against the process started for this review: GET /recall?q=... returned 200 in 9.419s, while /health warm is p50 5.8ms and /status p50 157ms. ask/check/recall all sit on the same substrate call. The split between auger's code and the substrate's embedding round trip was NOT instrumented, so that attribution is an inference.", "review_notes": null, "ts": null, "acceptance_criteria": "PASS: a repeated identical recall within one CLI session completes in under 500ms (cached query embedding), or the row records a measured breakdown proving the time is entirely outside auger. PASS: a user-visible progress line names the embedding step for slow calls, quoted from a real terminal transcript. FAIL: the same 9.4s figure reproduced for a repeat query with no cache and no message.", "complexity": 3, "created_at": "2026-11-12T00:39:51.024669+00:00", "updated_at": "2026-11-12T00:39:51.024669+00:00", "foreman_note": null, "capability_tags": ["perf", "recall", "ux"], "depends_on": [], "worker_status": "pending", "commit_hash": null, "guard_result": null, "ci_result": null, "worktree": null, "branch": null}
+{"status": "pending", "id": "REVIEW-AUGER-008", "title": "--domain refusal suggests the fixed 5th grid entry as if it were a match for the user's input", "detail": {"fingerprint": "a7bd6db0803812b6761d22cc5bb11c53c55de56dcaf4c473e571e234cabce6f6"}, "priority": "P4", "source": null, "reasoning": "For input 'delivery' the refusal prints 'Accepted: --domain 4.05 (4.05 is the data domain)'. The suggestion is grid[4] fixed, so every wrong input gets the same example, presented as if derived. The rest of the message is exemplary: it names the accepted shape and states that nothing was stored.", "review_notes": null, "ts": null, "acceptance_criteria": "PASS: the example is labelled 'e.g.' OR the hint fuzzy-matches the input against domain names and cites the closest canonical id. PASS: a transcript is quoted on the row showing input 'delivery' and the resulting message. FAIL: an unlabelled fixed index still presented as a match.", "complexity": 3, "created_at": "2026-11-12T00:39:51.07753+00:00", "updated_at": "2026-11-12T00:39:51.07753+00:00", "foreman_note": null, "capability_tags": ["cli", "validation", "error-message"], "depends_on": [], "worker_status": "pending", "commit_hash": null, "guard_result": null, "ci_result": null, "worktree": null, "branch": null}
+{"status": "pending", "id": "REVIEW-AUGER-009", "title": "a client that hangs up mid-response yields a phantom 502 in the log plus two chained tracebacks", "detail": {"fingerprint": "fab6f4a83ae8bdca84643e40324cb015e410faadb4abf9383a5e825d686cd2e0"}, "priority": "P4", "source": null, "reasoning": "Observed three times during a readiness poll with a 1s client timeout: GET /health answered 200, the client aborted during the write, the handler caught BrokenPipeError, attempted a 502 on the same closed socket, and printed two chained tracebacks. The server kept serving; the damage is a 502 line no client ever received.", "review_notes": null, "ts": null, "acceptance_criteria": "PASS: BrokenPipeError/ConnectionResetError around the response write are handled without emitting a status line or a traceback. PASS: a transcript is quoted on the row showing a 1s-timeout client run against a live server with zero tracebacks in the server log. FAIL: any phantom 5xx line for a client that never received it.", "complexity": 3, "created_at": "2026-11-12T00:39:51.132153+00:00", "updated_at": "2026-11-12T00:39:51.132153+00:00", "foreman_note": null, "capability_tags": ["api", "logging", "resilience"], "depends_on": [], "worker_status": "pending", "commit_hash": null, "guard_result": null, "ci_result": null, "worktree": null, "branch": null}
 {"status": "pending", "id": "AUG-168", "title": "Selection-scoped refusal misattributes an edge into a SKIPPED unreadable document as 'no block with that id'", "detail": {"fingerprint": "dd5a3c14da7293ef1d3edc61eb92df2e10f57bf55c475485bd0998589ae39e6b"}, "priority": "P3", "source": null, "reasoning": "Measured 2026-11-13 on 9702d49 (AUG-146 closeout). Corpus: a.xml with <requirement id=\"W-REQ-1\" depends-on=\"W-REQ-2\"> plus zz-broken.xml (truncated, contains id W-REQ-2). 'spec list <corpus> --id W-REQ-1' -> rc 2 'spec error (unresolved-reference): W-REQ-1 depends-on=W-REQ-2 (no block with that id)'; 'spec assemble --id W-REQ-1' -> same rc 2; 'spec validate' -> rc 2 invalid-xml naming the file. The refusal is correct but the diagnosis points at a MISSING BLOCK when the real cause is a document the same verb deliberately skipped (the AUG-146 tolerance). The two facts are already known to the loader (_spec_report_unreadable has the skipped list), so the message can name the skipped file instead of implying author error.", "review_notes": null, "ts": null, "acceptance_criteria": "PASS: with a corpus holding a valid document whose `depends-on` names a block inside a malformed sibling (`zz-broken.xml`), `PATH=$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH python3 auger.py spec list <corpus> --id <good-id>` exits 2 and its stderr NAMES the skipped file (the `zz-broken.xml` / `unreadable` token appears) alongside the `unresolved-reference` refusal. FAILIF: the refusal says only `(no block with that id)` with no mention of the unreadable document.\nPASS: `PATH=$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH python3 auger.py spec validate <corpus>` still exits 2 with `spec error (invalid-xml)` naming `zz-broken.xml`, so the corpus-wide refusal is unchanged. FAILIF: any other code or an unnamed file.\nPASS: a test in tests/test_xml_specs.py pins both directions and `grep -c \"tests/test_xml_specs.py\" tests/gate.sh` prints 2. FAILIF: 0 or 1 - the pinning suite dropped out of the gate pytest arm.\nPASS: `PATH=$PWD/.venv/bin:$HOME/.local/bin:$PATH bash tests/gate.sh` ends `GATE PASS` with exit 0. FAILIF: a non-zero exit or a required-arm skip.", "complexity": 2, "created_at": "2026-11-13T07:54:36.475844+00:00", "updated_at": "2026-11-13T07:54:36.475844+00:00", "foreman_note": null, "capability_tags": [], "depends_on": [], "worker_status": "pending", "commit_hash": null, "guard_result": null, "ci_result": null, "worktree": null, "branch": null}
